// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/server-sent-events.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeServerSentEvents(path: "/recipes/server-sent-events", title: "Listen to server-sent events — Recipes", description: "Receive a one-way flow of events from a server — prices, progress, a log — with a `stream` opened by `sse(…)`, and show the latest of each kind.") {
    RecipeShell("Listen to server-sent events", summary: "A `stream` receives a one-way flow of events from a server — prices, progress, a log — over server-sent events. Use it when the server talks and the page only listens; for two-way messages, [open a socket](/recipes/open-a-socket). This page shows the latest price as it arrives:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Open a socket", to: "/recipes/open-a-socket"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Talk to the site's other tabs", to: "/recipes/talk-between-tabs"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Connect two readers' pages", to: "/recipes/connect-two-readers")], source: "md-docs/recipes/server-sent-events.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** a server that sends events named `price` from `/events`.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Prices(path: "/prices", title: "Prices", description: "Live prices.") {
    state price = 0
    stream ticks = sse("/events", events: ["price"])
    effect { if let p = ticks.last("price") { price = p } }

    Heading("Prices").h1
    match ticks {
        open { Text("Price: {price}") }
        else { Text("Connecting…").muted }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- **`stream ticks = sse(\"/events\", events: [\"price\"])`** opens the stream when the page is drawn and closes it when the reader leaves. `events:` names the event types to listen for; only those names are listened to.\n- **`ticks.last(\"price\")`** is the latest event of that name. Each event name is kept apart, so it is the last price and not the last event of any kind; `ticks.last()` is the last unnamed message. The `effect` copies it into `price` each time a new one arrives.\n- **`match ticks`** reads the stream's state, with the same arms as a socket: `connecting`, `open`, `closed(c)`, `error(e)`, or an `else`.\n\n`ticks.messages` holds the messages in order — the last 500, or as many as `keep:` says. A message whose data parses as JSON arrives as a value.\n\nThe browser reconnects a stream on its own and resumes from the last event id the server sent. Pass `credentials: true` to send the site's cookies with the request.")

    }
}
